<title>USA: Colorado park district yields 6.25 pct in 2015.</title>
<headline>Colorado park district yields 6.25 pct in 2015.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>George K Baum said Tuesday it tentatively priced $6.45 million South Suburban Park and Recreation District, Colo., bonds at a top yield of 6.25 percent in 2015.</p>
<p>The preliminary pricing follows:</p>
<p>SOUTH SUBURBAN PARK AND RECREATION DISTRICT</p>
<p>ARAPAHOE DOUGLAS AND JEFFERSON COUNTIES, COLO.</p>
<p>RE: $6,450,000</p>
<p>GOLD COURSE AND ICE ARENA FACILITIES REVNEU REFUNDING AND</p>
<p>IMPROVEMENT BONDS, SERIES 1996</p>
<p>FIRST COUPON: 5/1/1997</p>
<p>DELIVERY FIRM: 9/30/1996</p>
<p>CALL OPTION: 11/1/2006 AT 101, DTP 2008, EXCEPT 11/1/2007</p>
<p>MATURITY</p>
<p>RATING: Baa</p>
<p>    5/1	     Amount	  Coupon	Price</p>
<p>    Maturity	(mln)	   (pct)	 (% of par)</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    1998	    $0.215	  4.80	  4.80</p>
<p>    1999	    $0.230	  5.00	  5.00</p>
<p>    2000	    $0.240	  5.20	  5.20</p>
<p>    2001	    $0.250	  5.30	  5.30</p>
<p>    2002	    $0.265	  5.40	  5.40</p>
<p>    2003	    $0.280	  5.50	  5.50</p>
<p>    2004	    $0.295	  5.60	  5.60</p>
<p>    2007	    $1.000	  6.00	  NRO</p>
<p>    2008	    $0.370	  6.00	  6.00</p>
<p>    2009	    $0.395	  6.00	  6.00</p>
<p>    2015	    $2.910	  6.00	  6.25</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
